@startuml
title OKS MCP Server — Query Sequence

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor User
participant "Coding Agent /\nMCP Client" as Agent
participant "SSH local\nport forward" as SSH
participant "MCP Server\n127.0.0.1:8001" as MCP
participant OksQueryService as Service
participant OksPipeline as Pipeline
participant "Schema +\nfew-shot retrieval" as Retrieval
participant "LLM API" as LLM
participant Validator
participant Executor
database "CVMFS TDAQ/OKS\ndata" as OKS

User -> Agent: Ask natural-language OKS question
Agent -> Agent: Resolve follow-up context
Agent -> SSH: MCP request to 127.0.0.1:18001/mcp
SSH -> MCP: Encrypted forwarded request
MCP -> Service: oks_query(question, version)
Service -> Service: Validate input and version
Service -> Pipeline: answer(..., interpret=false)
Pipeline -> Retrieval: Retrieve relevant schema slice
Retrieval --> Pipeline: Classes, attributes, relationships
Pipeline -> LLM: Translation prompt
LLM --> Pipeline: Candidate OksQuery / IR
Pipeline -> Validator: Validate against exact schema

alt Query invalid
  Validator --> Pipeline: Diagnostic
  Pipeline -> LLM: Repair prompt with diagnostic
  LLM --> Pipeline: Corrected OksQuery
  Pipeline -> Validator: Validate again
else Query valid
  Validator --> Pipeline: Valid query
end

Pipeline -> Executor: Execute approved OksQuery
Executor -> OKS: Read and filter selected data file
OKS --> Executor: Matching objects and attributes
Executor --> Pipeline: Structured results
Pipeline --> Service: Query, count, IDs, attributes, metadata
Service --> MCP: Bounded structured response
MCP --> SSH: MCP response
SSH --> Agent: Response through private tunnel
Agent --> User: Explain result

note over Agent, MCP
  No public listener is required.
  The server is stateless; the agent owns conversation memory.
end note
@enduml
